    {
      "id": "claim_9e87ca374f1f4875bdd6a01ec4daff23",
      "statement": "The bias decomposition identifies two components A = Cov(epsilon, eta) = w'Sigma P w (inflating Cov(y, z_hat)) and B = Var(eta) = w' P Sigma P w (inflating Var(z_hat)); placebo moments estimate A and B directly because placebo firms have Var(z)=0, yielding debiased slope beta_db = (Cov_tr - A) / (Var_tr - B).",
      "evidence": [
